---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="CSS Animations: A Complete Guide | Articles">
  <article class="article-page">
    <header class="article-header">
      <a href={`${base}articles/`} class="back-link">← Back to Articles</a>
      <h1 class="page-title">CSS Animations: A Complete Guide</h1>
      <div class="article-meta">
        <span>📅 January 5, 2024</span>
        <span>⏱️ 6 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="article-body content-box">
      <p>
        CSS animations are one of the most powerful tools in a web developer's arsenal.
        They can bring interfaces to life, guide users' attention, and create memorable
        experiences. Let's dive deep.
      </p>

      <h2>The Basics: Transitions vs Animations</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Transitions</strong> are simple: they animate between two states when
        a property changes. Perfect for hover effects and state changes.
      </p>

      <div class="code-box">
        <pre><code set:html={`.button {
  transition: transform 0.3s ease;
}
.button:hover {
  transform: scale(1.1);
}`} /></pre>
      </div>

      <p>
        <strong>Animations</strong> are more powerful: they can have multiple keyframes,
        run automatically, loop infinitely, and don't need a trigger.
      </p>

      <div class="code-box">
        <pre><code set:html={`@keyframes pulse {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  50% { opacity: 0.5; }
}
.element {
  animation: pulse 2s infinite;
}`} /></pre>
      </div>

      <h2>Timing Functions</h2>
      <p>
        The timing function (or "easing") controls the acceleration curve. It makes
        the difference between robotic movement and natural motion.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>linear</strong> — Constant speed (often looks unnatural)</li>
        <li><strong>ease</strong> — Slow start, fast middle, slow end</li>
        <li><strong>ease-in</strong> — Starts slow, ends fast</li>
        <li><strong>ease-out</strong> — Starts fast, ends slow</li>
        <li><strong>ease-in-out</strong> — Slow at both ends</li>
        <li><strong>cubic-bezier()</strong> — Custom curve</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Performance Tips</h2>
      <p>
        Not all CSS properties animate equally. For smooth 60fps animations, stick to:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>transform</strong> — translate, scale, rotate</li>
        <li><strong>opacity</strong> — fade in/out</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Avoid animating <code>width</code>, <code>height</code>, <code>top</code>,
        <code>left</code>, or <code>margin</code>. These trigger layout recalculations
        and will be janky on slower devices.
      </p>

      <h2>The Glow Effect</h2>
      <p>
        One of my favorite retro effects — the neon glow:
      </p>

      <div class="code-box">
        <pre><code set:html={`@keyframes glow {
  0%, 100% {
    text-shadow:
      0 0 10px #0ff,
      0 0 20px #0ff;
  }
  50% {
    text-shadow:
      0 0 20px #0ff,
      0 0 40px #0ff,
      0 0 60px #0ff;
  }
}
.neon-text {
  color: #0ff;
  animation: glow 2s ease-in-out infinite;
}`} /></pre>
      </div>

      <p>
        Layer multiple shadows at different blur radii for that authentic neon look.
        Combine with a dark background for maximum impact.
      </p>
    </div>

    <footer class="article-footer">
      <a href={`${base}articles/`} class="nav-btn">← More Articles</a>
    </footer>
  </article>

  <style>
    .article-page {
      max-width: 750px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .article-header {
      margin-bottom: 30px;
    }

    .back-link {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: var(--font-terminal);
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #666;
      text-decoration: none;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      transition: color 0.2s;
    }

    .back-link:hover {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .article-meta {
      display: flex;
      gap: 20px;
      justify-content: center;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #666;
      margin-top: 15px;
    }

    .article-body {
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .article-body h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-tech);
      font-size: 20px;
      color: var(--color-secondary);
      margin: 30px 0 15px;
      padding-left: 15px;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--color-secondary);
    }

    .article-body p {
      margin-bottom: 15px;
      color: #ccc;
    }

    .article-body strong {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .article-body code {
      background: #111;
      padding: 2px 6px;
      border-radius: 3px;
      font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--color-accent);
    }

    .article-body ul {
      margin: 20px 0;
      padding-left: 30px;
    }

    .article-body li {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      color: #bbb;
    }

    .article-body li::marker {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .code-box {
      background: #0a0a0f;
      border: 1px solid #333;
      border-radius: 5px;
      padding: 15px;
      margin: 20px 0;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    .code-box pre {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: #0f0;
    }

    .article-footer {
      margin-top: 40px;
      padding-top: 20px;
      border-top: 1px solid #333;
      text-align: center;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
